x hello.sh` — verify executable bit is set on disk\n+2. **Permission check (Git metadata)**: `git ls-files -s hello.sh` — confirm the staged file mode is `100755`, ensuring executable permissions are preserved across clones\n+3. **Shebang check**: `head -1 hello.sh` — confirm it starts with `#!/usr/bin/env bash`\n+4. **Output check**: `./hello.sh` — confirm stdout is exactly `Hello, World!`\n+5. **Exit code check**: Verify the script exits with status `0`\n+\n+Validation one-liner:\n+```bash\n+./hello.sh | diff - <(echo \"Hello, World!\") && echo \"PASS\" || echo \"FAIL\"\n+```\n+\n+Git permission validation:\n+```bash\n+git ls-files -s hello.sh | grep -q '^100755' && echo \"PASS\" || echo \"FAIL\"\n+```\n+\n+## Out of Scope\n+\n+- Argument parsing or parameterized greetings\n+- Localization / i18n\n+- Integration with any build system or CI pipeline\n+- Adding tests to a test framework (none exists in this project)\n+- Modifications to `README.md`\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/.ralph/ralph.toml b/.ralph/ralph.toml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..06625ad\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.ralph/ralph.toml\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+\n+# ralph workspace configuration\n+# The defaults are loaded from built-in values in the application and shown here\n+# for convenience so this file remains intentionally minimal.\n+[workspace]\ndiff --git a/.ralph/tmp/logs/issue-3-001-implementer.log b/.ralph/tmp/logs/issue-3-001-implementer.log\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..fa94840\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.ralph/tmp/logs/issue-3-001-implementer.log\n@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@\n+\n+--- attempt=1 backend=codex_gpt-5_4-high fallback=false ts=2026-03-18T22:03:04.837499484+00:00 ---\n+{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"019d02f9-4938-76a2-af9f-79a73b7f4c60\"}\n+{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"text\":\"**Preparing for updates**\\n\\nI need to provide short commentary updates before diving into substantial w